# LCOS menu patch for rEFInd 0.14.2.
# Installed as /usr/share/doc/lcos-bootmenu/lcos-menu.patch.
# Apply from the unpacked upstream tree:
#   patch -p1 < /usr/share/doc/lcos-bootmenu/lcos-menu.patch
#
# Short names under each OS icon (LCOS, Windows, Haiku, Linux, macOS),
# drawn by menu.c rather than one centered sentence. The tool row is
# shutdown, reboot, and firmware only: showtools is cleared by
# assignment, not SetMem, which left the stock About icon in place.
# Tool captions are not drawn; they overlap at the small icon size.
# The EFI binary built from this patch is /usr/lib/lcos-bootmenu/refind_x64.efi.

Rebuild (gnu-efi, x86_64):

    tar xf refind_0.14.2.orig.tar.gz
    cd refind-0.14.2
    patch -p1 < /usr/share/doc/lcos-bootmenu/lcos-menu.patch
    make gnuefi
    cp refind/refind_x64.efi /usr/lib/lcos-bootmenu/refind_x64.efi

Upstream: http://deb.debian.org/debian/pool/main/r/refind/refind_0.14.2.orig.tar.gz
The drivers (hfs) still come from Devuan's refind package. This binary
replaces only refind_x64.efi.
